# The Cessna 172P Skyhawk's checklists: this project's own, in its own words.
#
# **They are not taken from the aeroplane's flight manual.** No such
# manual was read to write them. What they follow is the ordinary
# practice for the type, in the order it is flown; the speeds and
# settings in them are this project's own figures, assets/figures/c172p.xml,
# whose sources docs/ASSETS.md records, and the flight model itself
# wherever the model is what decides - a lever's gate, a flap's travel,
# an engine's idle.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# The 172P's undercarriage is fixed and its propeller fixed-pitch, so nothing
# here names the gear or the pitch lever: an item that could never untick is
# not a check.

phase before-start
confirm Walk-round done, and the aeroplane is clear to start
confirm Seats upright, belts and harnesses fastened
confirm Fuel selector on both tanks
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Throttle open a quarter of an inch
confirm Master switch on, beacon on, and the propeller area called clear

phase taxi
check propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm >= 500 Engine running
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
confirm Brakes checked as the aeroplane first moves
confirm Compass and the turn coordinator checked in the turns
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.4 Taxi at a walking pace on low power

phase take-off
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 10.5 Flaps up, or ten degrees off a short field
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Elevator trim set for take-off
confirm Controls free and correct, and the instruments checked at full power
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Throttle wide open
check velocities/vc-kts >= 55.0 Lift the nose wheel at 55 knots

phase climb
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Throttle wide open
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
range velocities/vc-kts 70.0 90.0 Climb at 70 to 85 knots
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich below 3,000 feet
confirm Engine temperatures and pressures in the green

phase cruise
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.55 0.90 Power set between 55 and 75 per cent
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm <= 0.95 Mixture leaned for the cruising altitude
confirm Altimeter set, and the aeroplane trimmed to hold its height

phase descent
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.10 0.65 Power back for the descent
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.85 Mixture enriched as the aeroplane comes down
confirm Altimeter set to the field's pressure
confirm Cabin heat and air as wanted, and carburettor heat if it is needed

phase approach
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich
range velocities/vc-kts 60.0 80.0 Approach at 60 to 75 knots
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 30.5 Flaps as the approach needs, up to thirty degrees
confirm Landing light on, and the runway in sight

phase landing
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 20.0 30.5 Flaps twenty to thirty degrees
range velocities/vc-kts 55.0 70.0 Over the fence at 60 to 70 knots
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Throttle closed in the flare
confirm Touch down on the main wheels with the nose wheel held off

phase after-landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttle back to a taxi power
check velocities/vc-kts <= 30.0 Clear of the runway and slowed to a taxi
confirm Landing light off, and carburettor heat cold
